# .trivyignore: suppressions for the Trivy fs and image scans.
#
# Format: one CVE ID per line. Include a comment block above each
# group with the *why*, the *what's-the-real-mitigation*, and a
# *revisit date* so future-us can re-evaluate.
#
# DO NOT add a CRITICAL CVE here without explicit security review.
#
# Remove an entry as soon as its fix lands or its revisit date passes.
# A stale entry is worse than none: it silently hides that ID if it
# ever turns up in a real dependency. To check, run both scans without
# this file (see docs/security-ci.md).
#
# No active suppressions as of #170 (2026-10-17): the fs and image
# scans (Trivy v0.74.0, HIGH/CRITICAL, --ignore-unfixed) are clean
# without any. The 15 esbuild Go-stdlib entries that used to live here
# went stale when #56 / #163 removed esbuild, drizzle-kit and the
# TypeScript binary from the image; the fs scan skips node_modules and
# never matched them in the first place.
